  ORB ENTRY-FILTER TEST  --  filter 2 (RETEST) and filter 5 (DI), EACH SEPARATELY, vs the unfiltered baseline
======================================================================================================================================================
  RISK PARAMETERS (exact, from research/ftmo_engine.py):
    - fixed fractional, 1.00% of account equity risked per trade (RISK_PER_TRADE = 0.01)
    - stop = opposite side of the opening range; 1R = the OR width; UNCHANGED by either filter
    - targets: 1R, 2R, hold-to-session-close (stop live); ONE position per instrument per day, no pyramiding
  RETEST definition: after the first break, price must return to within 10% of the OR width of the broken
    level, within the SAME session; if a bar CLOSES back through the level first the day is CANCELLED
    (no immediate-entry fallback, no trade). Entry = limit fill at the broken OR level.
  DI definition: Wilder 14-period DMI on the SESSION (daily) bars, shifted 1 session (causal). Long only
    if +DI > -DI on the prior session, short only if -DI > +DI, else no trade.
  SESSION: US instruments = 09:30-16:00 America/New_York (per-bar DST-correct). BTCUSDT = 00:00-23:59 UTC
    (repo's existing crypto day boundary); 'session close' = the 23:59 UTC bar.
  COSTS: XAUUSD legacy $/oz | NAS100/US30 spread+0.35bps+ET-anchored slip 1.00/0.15 | BTCUSDT 20bps taker+slip
  NEW TRIALS THIS BATCH: 84  (72 filter cells + 12 first-time ORIGINAL cells for XAUUSD/BTCUSDT;
    NAS100/US30 ORIGINAL cells reproduce section 10 and are NOT re-counted)
  CUMULATIVE PROJECT TRIALS (DSR N): 946 + 84 = 1030
  DSR structural pool [in] = 48 filter cells -> E[max SR] +3.293 (mu -0.606, sd 1.725)
  DSR structural pool [out] = 24 filter cells -> E[max SR] +0.210 (mu -1.233, sd 0.729)
